        ".²1 A religious act of devotion or austerity, vowed observance, a vow in\n general; {#aByasyatIva vratamAsiDAram#} <ls>R. 13. 67</ls>, <ls n=\"R.\">2. 4</ls>, <ls n=\"R. 2.\">25</ls>; (there are\n several {%vratas%} enjoined in the different Purāṇas; but their number\n cannot be said to be fixed, as new ones, {%<ab>e. g.</ab>%} {#satyanArAyaRavrata#},\n are being added every day).\n",
        ".²2 A vow, promise, resolve; {#so'BUd BagnavrataH SatrUnudDftya pratiropayan#}\n <ls>R. 17. 42</ls>; so {#satyavrata, puRyavrata, dfQavrata#} <ab>&c.</ab>\n",
        ".²3 Object of devotion or faith, devotion; as in {#pativratA#} ({#patirvrataM#}\n {#yasyAH sA#}); {#yAnti devavratA devAn pitFn yAnti pitfvratAH#} <ls>Bg. 9. 25</ls>.\n",
        ".²4 A rite, an observance, practice, as in {#arkavrata#} <ab>q. v.</ab>; Śabaraswāmin\n defines it as {#puruzARAM kriyArTAnAM SarIraDAraRArTo balakaraRArTaScAyaM#}\n {#saMskAro vrataM nAma#} <ls>ŚB. on MS. 4. 3. 8</ls>.\n",
        ".²5 Mode of life, course of conduct; {#aTa tu vetsi Suci vratamAtmanaH#} <ls>Ś. 5. 27</ls>.\n",
        ".²6 An ordinance, a law, rule.\n",
        ".²7 Sacrifice.\n",
        ".²8 An act, deed, work.\n",
        ".²9 A design, plan.\n",
        ".²10 Mental activity; {#vratamiti ca mAnasaM karma ucyate#} <ls>ŚB. on MS. 6. 2. 20</ls>.\n",
        ".²11 Celibacy; {#vratalopanam#} <ls>Ms. 11. 61</ls> (<ab>com.</ab> {#brahmacAriRo BETunam#});\n <ls>Mb. 12. 11. 22</ls> (<ab>com.</ab> {#vrataM brahmacaryAdyupetamaDyayanam#}).\n"
